{
  "compatibilityLevel": 1604,
  "model": {
    "culture": "en-US",
    "defaultPowerBIDataSourceVersion": "powerBI_V3",
    "annotations": [
      {
        "name": "PBI_ProTooling",
        "value": "[\"RemoteModeling\", \"DirectLakeOnOneLakeCreatedInDesktop\"]"
      }
    ],
    "expressions": [
      {
        "name": "DirectLake",
        "kind": "m",
        "description": "Direct Lake connection to OneLake. The two GUIDs are workspace and item and are REWRITTEN at deploy time by duckrun's workspace.deploy(lakehouse=...); the pair checked in here is a PLACEHOLDER of zeros. Keep its SHAPE -- duckrun's _ONELAKE_REF matches 36 characters of hex and dashes and raises when nothing matches, and deploy_models._is_directlake_bim() greps the raw bytes for a onelake.dfs URL to decide this is a Direct Lake model at all. Removing the URL, or the camelCase mode token, silently turns it into something deploy cannot serve.",
        "expression": [
          "let",
          "    Source = AzureStorage.DataLake(\"https://onelake.dfs.fabric.microsoft.com/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000\", [HierarchicalNavigation=true])",
          "in",
          "    Source"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "tables": [
      {
        "name": "date_dim",
        "description": "The date dimension, 2,191 rows covering 2021-01-01..2026-12-31, marked as the model's date table (dataCategory Time). THE KEY COLUMN IS d_date, NOT d_date_sk_1: a Tabular table may carry at most ONE isKey column, and a marked date table requires it to be the DATE column -- both keyed is what Fabric rejected at create time on run 34563142340. d_date_sk_1 is still the relationship target for both facts (the paper's shifted key; d_date_sk is not in the model at all, so the substitution cannot be undone by accident), which needs uniqueness but not isKey. The time-intelligence measures name date_dim[d_date] explicitly, so they never depended on the marking.",
        "sourceLineageTag": "[mart].[date_dim]",
        "columns": [
          {
            "name": "d_date_sk_1",
            "dataType": "int64",
            "sourceColumn": "d_date_sk_1",
            "sourceLineageTag": "d_date_sk_1",
            "summarizeBy": "none"
          },
          {
            "name": "d_date",
            "dataType": "dateTime",
            "sourceColumn": "d_date",
            "sourceLineageTag": "d_date",
            "summarizeBy": "none",
            "formatString": "yyyy-MM-dd",
            "isKey": true
          },
          {
            "name": "d_year",
            "dataType": "int64",
            "sourceColumn": "d_year",
            "sourceLineageTag": "d_year",
            "summarizeBy": "none"
          },
          {
            "name": "d_qoy",
            "dataType": "int64",
            "sourceColumn": "d_qoy",
            "sourceLineageTag": "d_qoy",
            "summarizeBy": "none"
          },
          {
            "name": "d_moy",
            "dataType": "int64",
            "sourceColumn": "d_moy",
            "sourceLineageTag": "d_moy",
            "summarizeBy": "none"
          },
          {
            "name": "d_dow",
            "dataType": "int64",
            "sourceColumn": "d_dow",
            "sourceLineageTag": "d_dow",
            "summarizeBy": "none"
          },
          {
            "name": "d_dom",
            "dataType": "int64",
            "sourceColumn": "d_dom",
            "sourceLineageTag": "d_dom",
            "summarizeBy": "none"
          },
          {
            "name": "d_quarter_name",
            "dataType": "string",
            "sourceColumn": "d_quarter_name",
            "sourceLineageTag": "d_quarter_name",
            "summarizeBy": "none"
          }
        ],
        "dataCategory": "Time",
        "partitions": [
          {
            "name": "date_dim",
            "mode": "directLake",
            "source": {
              "type": "entity",
              "entityName": "date_dim",
              "expressionSource": "DirectLake",
              "schemaName": "mart"
            }
          }
        ]
      },
